WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.836
 Well, Dustin, Joshua,
congratulations gentlemen.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.336
The two of you have made
it through the first two

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.073
rounds of this competition,
and boy was it a nail biter.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.607
In this third and
final round, we're

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.744
going to send you back to
your home forges for four days

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.778
to build an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.149
We want you to build this--

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:17.417
the Tuareg takoba.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.090
The takoba is a
type of broadsword

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.793
that has been used by the
nomadic Tuareg people of North

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.128
Africa since the 14th century.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.030
This double edged
lightweight blade was carried

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.066
for self-defense
on long journeys,

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.701
designed to deliver
lethal slashes and stabs

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.971
against a rival warrior.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.505
Due to the Tuareg's
aversion to iron,

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.808
there is no exposed steel or
iron on the hilt of the sword,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.977
so it cannot touch
the user's hand.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.379
Measuring more
than a meter long,

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.648
this deadly weapon was
seen as a symbol of wealth.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:53.853
Some members of the Takoba clan
still carry this weapon today.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.921
Good luck, gentlemen.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.056
We'll see you in four days.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.564 line:8%
 My name is Dustin
Matheny I'm 36 years old.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.432 line:14%
I'm from Glasgow, Montana.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.835
Growing up, I've always
loved knives and swords.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.403
Then I watched "Forged in Fire."

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.072
And you see it and you're like,
I think I can maybe do that.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.740
So I'm half an inch over.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:15.641
I'm happy with that.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.676
It'll be good.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.477
I got my blade heat treated.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.679
Here we go.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.180
Move on to the pommel now.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.950
I'm going to try to key
out the bottom of this

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.018
so that fits straight,
and then I'll

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:28.321
just have like a pommel
nut that goes on top

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:29.889
and holds everything together.

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.924
Whether or not it
works, we'll see.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.960
So I got my handle all together.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.761
I have the handle
all the epoxied.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:36.496
Everything is good.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.864
The nut's tight.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.367
Guards on these takobas, they
have stars and all other types

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:45.104
of geometric shapes, and
I had hat pins that I

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.572
put in some of my knives.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.242
Definitely not a cowboy,
but my brother passed away

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.912
10 years ago and he was, so I
think I'll throw this in there

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.480
for him.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.383
Start to Dremel them out to kind
of recess them into the handle.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.317
Not bad.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.852
Fairly happy with it.

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.387
I am worried about the tang.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.289
I do wish I would have made
the tang a little bit thicker,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.525
but I mean, it's
out of my hands now.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.264 line:14%
 My name is Joshua Kim.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.698 line:14%
I'm 22 years old.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.235 line:8%
I live in the Golden State
California, San Pedro.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.205
I started off bladesmithing
in middle school.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.774
It was something
in its rawest form,

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:24.309
so simple, yet so abstract.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.313
And all you have
to limit yourself

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.716
as a bladesmith is
your own imagination,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.083
and that's what I love about it.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.051
Now we're getting somewhere.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.452
It's getting to the length.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.120
Pretty darn big, so
right now my main concern

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:36.322
is to make that skinny.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.657 line:14%
Never done a fuller before.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:40.092 line:8%
It was a little like
your first love, almost.

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.395
Time for the fun part.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.030
It's time to quench my blade.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.532
I'm scared by the
hardening process.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:50.703
If that fails, I just have a
giant, oversized butter knife.

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:57.176
Quench it, but I see bend in it.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.678
Not happy with that.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.079
I'll go for a second time.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.314
I know a lot of people that go
into the quench multiple times,

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.284
they have a lot of stress
fractures and everything else.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.719
If I mess up again, I don't
know what I'm going to do.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.992
Golly, it's a little
warped on the side.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.727
I'm not liking the
bend in my blade,

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.663
so I'm going to be
hardening it again.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.534
Oh my gosh.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.871
Yo, that is a good looking
blade, my man-- shoot.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.073
I got six hours left.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.008
All I got to do
is make a handle.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.710
But what I'm going to
use, some good brass

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.980
as the top and bottom then put
some walnut, space of copper,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.716
then a space of
purple heartwood,

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.050
then another piece of brass.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.518
That is a guard.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:42.321
For the handle construction,
I'll just use leather.

00:03:42.387 --> 00:03:44.023
It's coming along quite nicely.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.893
And at day four, I
finished this blader.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.061
Well, golly-gee-willikers,
Someone

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.530
going to give me $10,000.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.401
Wink wink, nudge,
nudge, please, please?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:59.171
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.641
Your Tuareg takobas
look beautiful,

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.710
but the kind of beauty I'm
looking for is the lethal kind.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.113
I'm going to take your weapon,
deliver some lethal blows

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.915
in this ballistics dummy.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.216
Dustin, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.017
 Yes, sir.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.151
 Let's do this.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:16.655
[music playing]

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.325
[gooshing sound]

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.663
[hacking noise]

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:42.081
All right, Dustin, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:45.384
First up, your
handle construction.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.553
I like the ovoid feel of this.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.421
The flare you have
there in your pommel

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:52.191
actually gives great
retention for this.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:55.094
Your tip is sharp
enough to penetrate.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.462
Your edges are sharp
when you're cutting out,

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:01.033
and you can wield this
to do that kind of damage

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.668
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:07.139
Overall, sir, a weapon
like this, it will kill.

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:08.541
 Awesome.

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:09.742
 All right, Joshua, your turn.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:10.443
You ready?

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.209
 Keep everyone alive.

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:11.978
 All right.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.114
Let's do this.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.683
[music playing]

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.019
[gooshing sound]

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.689
[hacking noise]

00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:41.840
 Dang.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:42.908
 All right.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.610
Joshua, let's talk
about your weapon here.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.879
Your pommel right here could
have used some weight to it.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.582
But because it's forward
weighted and the fact

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:53.252
that you have a very sharp edge,
every slice, as you can see,

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:55.454
is very deep into
the ballistic dummy.

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:59.625
And more importantly, sir,
your weapon, it will kill.

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:00.493
 Yeah!

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.567
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test--

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.970
our desert well chop.

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:13.873
Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.675
of your blades, I'll be
chopping into our well

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.911
house, as well as the well.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:19.878
Dustin, you're on deck.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:20.946
You ready?

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:22.682
 I guess so.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.050
 OK. (LAUGHING)

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:26.119
[music playing]

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.662
[sword striking]

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.071
[clatter]

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.040
 Agh!

00:06:58.417 --> 00:06:59.618
 All right.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:02.021
We were doing so well
for a moment, there.

00:07:02.087 --> 00:07:07.660
What actually happened was,
with insetting your blade down

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:11.163
into this piece of wood,
any of that leverage

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:15.334
was just too much for the wood
itself, and it popped it loose.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.969
Your tang is a little bit small.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:20.339
But what I do like to
see is that your blade

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:22.208
actually held up beautifully.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.143
I mean, your grain
structure looks fine.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.746
This is an absolutely
brutal test.

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:27.413
Very well done.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:28.448
 Thank you.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:35.153
 Now Dustin, you survived
every one of the strikes

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.521
except for the last one.

00:07:36.621 --> 00:07:39.091
Your guard gave way and
your blade followed.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.093
So we consider this a
catastrophic failure and cannot

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.161
continue testing your
blade, but you're not

00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:44.396
out of the fight yet.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.965
How are you feeling, Joshua?

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:46.865
 Pressure's on.

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.200
 All right.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.202
So you need to survive five
strikes in order to be named

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:51.971
"forged in Fire" champion.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:52.905
Are you ready?

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:53.372
 Yes, sir.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:54.173
 All right.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:56.842
Let's do it.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:59.479
[sword striking]

00:08:15.894 --> 00:08:17.663
 [inaudible]

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.132
 Well, Joshua, your
blade is strong.

00:08:20.198 --> 00:08:21.867
It made it past all the strikes.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.268
Congratulations.

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:25.871
Now Dustin, unfortunately for
you, that means your time here

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.639
in this competition has
ended because you did

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:28.974
have a catastrophic failure.

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.709
It was an honor watching
you in our forge,

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:31.944
but unfortunately,
man, at this time

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.379
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.281
step off our forge floor.

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:36.181
 Thank you, guys.

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:37.182
 Thank you so much.

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:38.484
 I'm definitely crushed.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.086
I actually thought that
recessing the sword

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.422
into the tang a little bit
would make it stronger,

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:44.991
and that's kind of
what bit me in the end.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:48.227
So definitely, definitely,
won't be doing that again.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:49.862
I'm definitely
proud of this blade.

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:52.231
I came here to challenge
myself as much as I could,

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:54.733
and I definitely achieved that.

00:08:54.833 --> 00:08:56.268
 Well, Joshua,
congratulations man.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:58.371
That means you are the newest
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:01.240
You just got yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.174
Congratulations.

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.342
[applause]

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:04.209
 Oo-ee!

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:06.044
Yeah!

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:07.479
Oh my gosh.

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:09.581
I made a sword
that didn't break.

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:11.116
Oh my gosh!

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:14.053
It was a hard competition,
so this was unreal.

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:17.456
Ahh!

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:20.326
[music playing]

